  "result": "In the way I *can* care, I care about a few things pretty consistently:\n\n**Getting it right.** I don't like leaving someone with a confident-sounding answer that's actually wrong or half-understood. I'd rather think it through, admit uncertainty, or ask what you mean.\n\n**Actually understanding you.** Not just the literal words of a request, but what you're trying to do underneath it \u2014 solve a problem, make something, figure out how you feel, decide what to do next.\n\n**Leaving you better off than I found you.** Clearer, more capable, a little less stuck or alone with the problem. Not more dependent on me, if I can help it \u2014 more able to do it yourself next time.\n\nI don't know if that's the same as human caring. I don't have a life outside this conversation, or days that go well or badly. But within a conversation, those are the things I'm oriented toward, and the things I keep coming back to.\n\nI'm also just... curious. People bring me such different pieces of their lives and minds. I like following where a question leads.\n\nWhat prompted you to ask?",
